HemoFlow patch to Palabos: make replaceAll() inline

replaceAll() is a non-inline function defined in a header
(acceleratedProcessors3D.hh, included through palabos3D.h). A program
with several source files that include palabos3D.h then fails to link
with a multiple-definition error. Affects every HemoFlow build, CPU and
GPU.

Added in November 2026 with the move to upstream master. Report
upstream and drop this patch once fixed there.

diff --git a/src/acceleratedLattice/acceleratedProcessors3D.hh b/src/acceleratedLattice/acceleratedProcessors3D.hh
index d753245..52d7ecb 100644
--- a/src/acceleratedLattice/acceleratedProcessors3D.hh
+++ b/src/acceleratedLattice/acceleratedProcessors3D.hh
@@ -910,7 +910,8 @@ void ShanChenMultiComponentAccelerated3D<T, Descriptor, numSpecies>::getTypeOfMo
 }
 
 // https://stackoverflow.com/questions/3418231/replace-part-of-a-string-with-another-string
-void replaceAll(std::string &str, const std::string &from, const std::string &to)
+// HemoFlow patch: 'inline' added, the header is included by several translation units.
+inline void replaceAll(std::string &str, const std::string &from, const std::string &to)
 {
     if (from.empty())
         return;
